WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.070
A phone in one country,
a laptop in another,

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.570
from different makers.

3
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.010
They've never met.

4
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.090
Yet when the phone emails a
photo, it arrives perfectly.

5
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:15.770
Zoom in: before it leaves, the photo is
wrapped and passed down a stack of trays.

6
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.210
So how do two machines that have
never met agree how to talk?

7
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.470
In this mission, you'll learn that a
protocol is a set of rules for transferring

8
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.370
data.

9
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.330
You'll see that different
jobs use different protocols,

10
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.910
like SMTP for sending email.

11
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.170
And you'll find out why the
job is divided into layers,

12
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.170
each doing one part.

13
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.440
Your mission: explain how two computers
that have never met agree how to talk.
